{
	title: 'Providers see one Action tool with leased READ/EDIT/WRITE and HELP',
	spec: "Providers see one native tool, Action { action: string }. Its text is NAME, an optional /* purpose */ comment, then arguments: JS string literals or ASON objects. Each tools/ module declares its Action form (positional fields, summary, usage) next to its definition; actions.ts resolves Action text to the module call, and SYSTEM.md's $tools_summary lists enabled modules from the registry. HELP <NAME> renders precise help from the module's own definition, never a parallel dictionary. A malformed Action fails as a tool error naming the problem and the raw text; nothing runs. History stores the resolved call plus the original text; replay sends providers the Action text (older native calls as NAME { fields }). READ of a text file returns numbered lines and a whole-file lease path@hash; EDIT takes path@hash and {range, lines} blocks, applied atomically in one write; a stale hash writes nothing and shows the current lines around each range. WRITE creates or replaces a whole file atomically. EDIT and WRITE record file changes like bash modifies. BASH keeps background, unsafeToStop, modifies and approval. SYSTEM.md supports $name and ${name} variables.",
